    {
      "id": "antony-and-cleopatra/sceneIV_3.12/p@171226",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "SCARUS.\nSwallows have built\nIn Cleopatra’s sails their nests. The augurs\nSay they know not, they cannot tell; look grimly,\nAnd dare not speak their knowledge. Antony\nIs valiant and dejected, and by starts\nHis fretted fortunes give him hope and fear\nOf what he has and has not.",
